commit 9a26dbddaf24eb96f2c09918c1619dd3456924fa

C03: a go-to order whose destination ends in a bare article asks which portal (DIALOGUE1491)

The owner marked «Ve a portal una.» and «Ve Portal 2 UN» as messages cut by the transcription: understand from context or ask. With no context the product searched «portal una» (an honest failure) or sent «Ve Portal 2 UN» to the model. `_unresolved_input_kind` now reads a go-to/open order whose portal, page or site name ends in a bare article or preposition as the `cut_destination` kind; `clarify_unresolved_input` composes one short question that says the name seems cut and asks which portal or site to go to, validated (it must ask which portal/page/site, never complete or guess the destination) with one corrected retry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


